# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the fuzzers: known library leaks, so
# that a fuzzing run is not stopped by them.  Remove an entry when its
# bug is fixed.  See also ../lsan.supp.

# XmString.c: _XmStringNonOptCreate() leaks the rendition tag arrays of
# every segment that has rendition components (finish_segment() copies
# its stack record and resets it without freeing them); the XmString
# suite's byte_stream_rendition_leak case checks this one.
leak:_XmStringNonOptCreate

# The same as in ../lsan.supp.
leak:XtOwnSelection
leak:XtDisownSelection
leak:_XmSFAddNavigator

# Mrmappl.c, MrmFetchWidgetOverride: when UrmCreateWidgetTree() fails
# (a corrupt .uid), the widget reference context made by
# Urm__CW_InitWRef() and the SetValues list are not freed.
leak:Urm__CW_InitWRef
leak:ClipboardGetByNameItem

# XmStringFunc.c, XmStringToXmStringTable: the rendition list of its
# string context (XmString.c, begin_context_rends) is not freed for some
# strings with rendition tags; crashes/xmstring/table-rendition-context-leak.
leak:begin_context_rends

# ResEncod.c, XmCvtCTToXmString: the separator it caches for newlines
# leaks for some inputs with direction sequences between newlines, for
# example c9 c9 0a 0a 0a 27 0a 0a 0a 0a 0a 9b 5d 0a 0a ff ff.  Only a
# leak check right after the conversion sees it (it is not reported at
# exit), so there is no crashes/ct replay.  Not narrowed down further.
leak:XmStringSeparatorCreate
